{
    "_type": "Project",
    "_id": "MEDACCESS-PROJECT",
    "name": "MedAccess",
    "documentation": "MedAccess - State Diagram Model (STD-01 .. STD-06).\nMedAccess is a pharmacist-supervised medicine information and availability assistant. It is not an online pharmacy, a diagnostic system, a prescribing system, a medicine-delivery service, an autonomous substitution system or a payment/purchasing system.\nNo state diagrams are modelled for Price, Medicine, Role, AuditLogEntry, Pharmacy or VerificationComment - the SRS does not establish meaningful lifecycle states for them.",
    "ownedElements": [
        {
            "_type": "UMLModel",
            "_id": "MEDACCESS-MODEL",
            "_parent": {
                "$ref": "MEDACCESS-PROJECT"
            },
            "name": "MedAccess State Machines",
            "documentation": "Recommended state diagram set for the MedAccess MVP:\nSTD-01 User Account (User)\nSTD-02 Potential Medicine Match (PotentialMedicineMatch)\nSTD-03 Medicine Comparison (MedicineComparison)\nSTD-04 Incorrect Information Report (IncorrectInformationReport)\nSTD-05 Refill Reminder (RefillReminder)\nSTD-06 Pharmacy Availability (PharmacyAvailability)",
            "ownedElements": [
                {
                    "_type": "UMLStateMachine",
                    "_id": "STD01",
                    "_parent": {
                        "$ref": "MEDACCESS-MODEL"
                    },
                    "name": "STD-01 User Account State",
                    "documentation": "Object: User\nPurpose: Model the lifecycle/status of a MedAccess user account.\nRelated Requirements: FR-01-FR-04, FR-35, NFR-01-NFR-03, FR-38-FR-39.\nTraceability: AD-01 Authenticate User / AD-08 User & Role Management; SD-01, SD-08.\nRule: Account status and role are different concepts. Roles (Patient, Caregiver, Pharmacist, Pharmacy Staff, Doctor/Healthcare Professional, Administrator) are NOT modelled as states.\nNote: A 'Suspended' state is deliberately omitted - requirements do not explicitly establish suspension.\nNote: No final state is used - the lifecycle does not genuinely terminate in the SRS.",
