                {
                    "_type": "UMLStateMachine",
                    "_id": "STD04",
                    "_parent": {
                        "$ref": "MEDACCESS-MODEL"
                    },
                    "name": "STD-04 Incorrect Information Report State",
                    "documentation": "Object: IncorrectInformationReport\nPurpose: Model the lifecycle of a report concerning potentially incorrect medicine price or availability information.\nRelated Requirements: FR-28-FR-31, FR-38-FR-39.\nTraceability: AD-06 Report & Resolve Incorrect Information; SD-06.\nCRITICAL RULE: a submitted report never causes an automatic stock/price change. The flow is submission -> authorized review -> investigation -> resolution -> audit record. The report workflow is separate from the underlying stock/price update workflow.\nNote: 'Investigating' may be omitted if the Activity Diagram does not distinguish investigation from review.",
