                    "name": "STD-06 Pharmacy Availability State",
                    "documentation": "Object: PharmacyAvailability\nPurpose: Model the reported availability state of a medicine at a participating pharmacy.\nRelated Requirements: FR-10-FR-14, NFR-13-NFR-14, BR-05.\nTraceability: AD-02 Pharmacy Availability & Price Comparison / AD-04 Update Medicine Stock; SD-02, SD-04.\nThe SRS explicitly defines the states Available, Low Stock and Unavailable. Because pharmacy staff can update availability repeatedly, transitions may occur in either direction rather than as a one-way lifecycle.\nTIMESTAMP RULE: availability state does not itself communicate freshness. The PharmacyAvailability data must also retain/report source and last-updated time (state diagram -> availability status; class/data model -> status + source + timestamp). Availability must not be represented as guaranteed real-time inventory.",
